<section class="faq-section wrap"><div><div class="section-kicker">A LITTLE MORE CONTEXT</div><h2>Good to know.</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is this the official Rocket.Chat client?</summary><p>No. AmiRocket is an independent native client for AmigaOS. Rocket.Chat is the name of the chat platform it connects to.</p></details><details><summary>How does it receive new messages?</summary><p>AmiRocket polls the server’s REST API. The interval is configurable. It does not currently use realtime WebSocket updates.</p></details><details><summary>Can I connect it to NovaDock?</summary><p>The ARexx control and notification interfaces are available for integration development. A finished NovaDock widget is a separate integration, not included in this release.</p></details><details><summary>Where are my settings stored?</summary><p>The client and Preferences share ENVARC:AmiRocket.prefs, including server and plugin settings. Remember login stores an authentication token, never your password. Keep this file private.</p></details></div></section>
